# Koa Routing And Repositories

- Mount new HTTP surfaces through `Routes/unprotected-repositories.js` or `Routes/protected-repositories.js`; adding a route file alone is not enough.
- Preserve `server.js` boot order: unprotected routes before `koa-jwt`, protected routes after it.
- Match the existing repository shape under `Repositories/<Feature>/` and keep business logic out of route declarations.
- Prefer the backend flow `route -> controller -> module -> model/middleware`.
- If an older script or note mentions `api.routes.js`, treat that as stale and use the `Routes/*-repositories.js` registries instead.

## Required Repository format (Miguel, 2026-10-16)

Every new feature mirrors `Repositories/ZelfID` / `Repositories/Tags`:

- Folders: `Repositories/<Feature>/{routes,middlewares,controllers,modules,models}`; files named `<feature>.routes.js`, `<feature>.middleware.js`, `<feature>.controller.js`, `<feature>[-part].module.js`, `<thing>.model.js`.
- **routes**: wiring only, `server.<verb>(\`${PATH}/x\`, Middleware.xValidation, Controller.x)` with `const PATH = config.basePath(base)`. **No inline async handlers in routes.**
- **middlewares**: Joi validation via `Core/JoiUtils` (`validate(schema, …)`, `409 { validationError }` on failure), plus auth/guard checks; they set `ctx.state` / normalise `ctx.request.body` and call `next()`.
- **controllers**: only ctx in/out; `try { const data = await Module.x(...); ctx.body = { data }; } catch (error) { const _exception = errorHandler(error, ctx); ctx.status = _exception.status; ctx.body = { message: _exception.message, code: _exception.code }; }`.
- **modules**: all business logic; throw `"NNN:code"` errors (optionally with `clientCode`) for `Core/http-handler` `errorHandler`.
- Register in `Routes/unprotected-repositories.js` or `Routes/protected-repositories.js`.

